# Historic Runbook Execution Guidance

- Document Marlowe benchmark/eval commands as Slurm submissions (`sbatch`), not direct long-running CLI invocations on login nodes.
- Prefer `scripts/slurm/` wrappers and include concrete examples users can copy.
- For every execution section, include:
  - repo sync step (`cd /projects/m000102/code/levante-bench && git pull`)
  - exact submit command
  - where to watch job state/logs (`squeue`, Slurm output path)
- Keep direct interactive commands limited to diagnostics or short smoke checks.
